.env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operational databases.
#
# These are the *live* stores: they are rebuilt by fetching from the Blizzard
# API and they are measured in gigabytes.  Git is a source-code tool; a
# 4.4 GB binary blob in a commit is not reviewable, cannot be diffed, and
# makes every clone and every push pay for data that is derived anyway.
# The schema lives in code (`woweconomy/intel/store.py`), so a fresh checkout
# recreates an empty store and refills it with `scripts/intel.py`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
archives/
data/aggregates.sqlite
data/aggregates.sqlite-wal
data/aggregates.sqlite-shm

# Runtime state.  A lock file or a cursor position describes this machine at
# this second; committing it means the next pull fights the running pipeline.
data/watch.lock
data/watch_state.json
data/export_state.json

# Written by the export next to the dataset it describes: the checksum and
# counts of one run, not the dataset itself (which stays tracked).
DFA_Estimate/Data/DFA_Estimate_Data.meta.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data for Azeroth cache and exports.
#
# `woweconomy/dfa/` is the default cache location for the Blizzard collection
# scrapers (`services/blizzard_collections.py`) and one of the folders the
# reports look in for `demand_*.csv`.  On this workstation the real folder is
# named by `DFA_DIR`; what lands here is a cache, and a cache is derived.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
woweconomy/dfa/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reading passes over the code.
#
# These audits (`*_report.txt`, `module_consumption*`, the `*-map.md` files)
# were written by one-off reviews of the module graph.  They are not
# documentation the project maintains, and a fresh pass would otherwise add
# another untracked file each time.  Reviewed analysis that should live in the
# repo goes under `reports/`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/cross_reference_report.txt
/farmanalysis-implementation-report.md
/final_root_consumption_note.txt
/free_name_usage_report.txt
/module_consumption_report.md
/module_consumption_summary.txt
/module_usage_summary.json
/pipeline-deadcode-analysis.md
/woweconomy-diagnostic-report.md
/woweconomy_module_analysis.md
woweconomy/farmanalysis-ph1-backend-store-mapping.md
woweconomy/persistence-map.md
woweconomy/sqlite-map.md
woweconomy/sqlite-references.md


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dated dumps and published game files.
#
# `data/tsm/snapshots/<stamp>/` is one TSM sweep: ~250 CSVs per stamp and
# 387 MB on this machine, regenerated by `scripts/fetch_tsm_snapshots.py`.
# `data/game/` is what `scripts/watch_addons.py` publishes out of the game's
# SavedVariables so the container can read the journal.  Both describe a run
# rather than the code, and a new stamp should not turn every `git status`
# into 250 untracked paths.
#
# An ignore rule does not evict an index entry, so the stamps committed before
# this line stay tracked; they simply stop accumulating.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/tsm/snapshots/
data/game/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build and test detritus.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/

# Logs: appended by whatever ran last, never a source of truth.
logs/
*.log

# Dated CSV backups written by the export scripts (`items.2026-10-21.bak.csv`).
csv/*.bak.csv
reports/**/*.bak.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local scratch.  `attic/` holds the one-off probes and measurements that used
# to sit at the repo root; they are kept for reference but are not part of the
# system.  `data/_phase*` holds pre-migration backups and experiment output.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/_*.py
/_*.txt
/_*.json
/file
storage_audit*.json
storage_audit*.txt
attic/
data/_phase*/
# A model bundle is published by writing a `.staging-*` directory and then
# renaming it into place, so an interrupted train leaves one behind.  It is
# by definition incomplete -- ignoring it by name is safer than a blanket
# `*.joblib`, which would drop a bundle's calibrators while keeping its
# manifest and leave a version that loads and then fails.
models/**/.staging-*

# Written analysis lives in `reports/` and is tracked.  The JSON that the
# rehearsal and evaluation scripts emit is not: it contains absolute paths
# and byte counts from this machine, so a committed copy is wrong the next
# time anyone runs the script.  Regenerate it.
/dryrun_*.json
/runtime_baseline.json
/retention_dryrun.json
reports/mog_eval.json
reports/space_baseline.json
reports/step3_archive_only.json

# Assistant session state (memory notes), not project source.
.workbuddy-ai/

# Editor / OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
reports/dryrun_*.json
